[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ETH-W5500 Extension High-Level Software Requirements
UID: ETH-SW
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Implementation independent requirements on any firmware that uses the
W5500 extension. They refine KM271-SW-013.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Driver and start-up

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-001
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: SPI driver
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall drive the W5500 on the SPI pins of J7 (v2.0: SCLK 12, MOSI
11, MISO 13, CS 10) with configurable pins and a clock of at most the value
that runs stable on the board (default 20 MHz).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SW-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYA-100

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-002
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Reset before initialisation
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall pulse RSTn (v2.0: GPIO16) low for at least 500 us and wait
for the W5500 to become ready before initialising it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYA-202
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-HW-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-003
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Interrupt
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should use the W5500 interrupt on GPIO14 instead of polling.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYA-100

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-004
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: No I2C with the extension
STATEMENT: >>>
When the Ethernet extension is enabled, the firmware shall not use I2C on
SDA/SCL of J7.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYA-202

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Network behaviour

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-010
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Address configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall support DHCP and a static IPv4 configuration on the
Ethernet interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SW-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-011
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Fallback to WiFi
STATEMENT: >>>
If Ethernet has no link or no IP address, the device shall stay reachable over
WiFi (station or setup access point).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SW-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-012
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: WiFi off while Ethernet is connected
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware should offer an option to switch WiFi off while Ethernet has an
IP address and to restart WiFi when the Ethernet connection is lost.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
W5500 (about 130 mA) plus active WiFi with TX peaks can cause brown-outs on
weak Logamatic supplies.
<<<
SOURCE: eth-wifi-off-2026-11-25 (dewenni feature proposal)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SW-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-013
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: PHY power-down when unused
STATEMENT: >>>
When Ethernet is disabled in the configuration, the firmware should put the
W5500 PHY into power-down mode.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Without a cable the W5500 draws about 75 mA during auto-negotiation, about 13
mA in power-down.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SW-014
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Link status
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report the Ethernet link state, speed and IP address as
status values.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-004

[[/SECTION]]
